  "tours": [
    {
      "id": "tour:hmr",
      "title": "How Vite chooses a hot update, reload, or no update",
      "summary": "For each affected development environment, Vite checks the changed modules and their importers. Accepting boundaries produce targeted updates. Empty module sets, dead ends, circular invalidation, and client HTML template changes cause a reload. An unanalyzed module can yield no update payload, in which case Vite sends no update message.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "t1",
          "view": "view:hmr",
          "focus": [
            "hmr:1"
          ],
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/vite/src/node/server/index.ts",
              "span": {
                "from": 912,
                "to": 912
              },
              "role": "call-site"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/vite/src/node/server/hmr.ts",
              "symbol": "handleHMRUpdate",
              "span": {
                "from": 245,
                "to": 245
              },
              "role": "definition"
            }
          ],
          "note": "### A changed file starts a boundary search\n\nThe server forwards changed files to the update handler. For each affected environment, the handler passes matched modules to the update decision.",
          "editor": {
            "primary": "packages/vite/src/node/server/hmr.ts"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-empty",
          "view": "view:hmr",
          "focus": [
            "hmr:8"
          ],
          "note": "### An empty module set reloads\n\nWhen a root module invalidates itself, the module list can be empty. Vite marks that case for a full reload before walking any importers.",
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/vite/src/node/server/hmr.ts",
              "symbol": "updateModules",
              "find": "let needFullReload: HasDeadEnd = modules.length === 0",
              "role": "definition"
            }
          ],
          "editor": {
            "primary": "packages/vite/src/node/server/hmr.ts"
          }
        },
