              "symbol": "propagateUpdate",
              "find": "if (node.id && node.isSelfAccepting === undefined) {",
              "role": "definition"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/vite/src/node/server/hmr.ts",
              "symbol": "propagateUpdate",
              "find": "if (!node.importers.size) {",
              "role": "definition"
            }
          ],
          "note": "### The importer search can stop in three ways\n\nA module can accept its own change or an importer can accept its dependency. A loaded module with no accepting boundary and no importer is a dead end. An unanalyzed module stops propagation without declaring a dead end; if it yields no update payload, Vite sends no update.",
          "editor": {
            "primary": "packages/vite/src/node/server/hmr.ts"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-circular",
          "view": "view:hmr",
          "focus": [
            "hmr:9"
          ],
          "note": "### A circular invalidation reloads\n\nWhen an accepted boundary leads back to the module that first invalidated this update, Vite chooses a full reload instead of sending that boundary's update.",
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/vite/src/node/server/hmr.ts",
              "symbol": "updateModules",
              "find": "firstInvalidatedBy &&",
              "role": "definition"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/vite/src/node/server/hmr.ts",
